Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::the_entry_array_check_is_total`.

The defect: the entry size is checked for a multiple of eight and not for its lower bound, so a
header that declares entries of 0 or 8 bytes passes, and the partition check that follows slices
a 128-byte entry past the end of the array it was given.

Expected to fail: the assertion that an accepted array is one 128-byte entry, on a header that
declares one entry of 8 bytes.
